  "summary": "Applied ML / LLM scientist leading graph-aware search and entity understanding for an Amazon-scale knowledge graph. Drove LLM distillation from large proprietary models (e.g. Claude-class) to smaller open-weight (including multimodal) models to enable low-latency online serving with drastic cost reductions, validated via LLM-as-a-judge evaluation. Built high-precision entity resolution and entity linking pipelines and standardized ER across heterogeneous catalogs to power Alexa- and retail-facing experiences. Defined measurement that connects search/navigation engagement to downstream business outcomes and used it to drive doc-driven, cross-functional decisions. Targeting ML/LLM leadership roles where retrieval, knowledge graphs, and productionizing LLMs actually move the needle.",
